WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE Simulated excerpt: a synthesized voice reading text written for the demo. CloudBridge Summit 2026 is a fictional event.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
[Simulated excerpt: synthesized voice, fictional speaker]

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.540
<v Ananya Iyer>Our internal developer portal had a search box that everyone ignored. Here is why.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.180
<v Ananya Iyer>Keyword search was great when you knew the exact words.

4
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.960
<v Ananya Iyer>Type the error code E4031 and the runbook came up first.

5
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.920
<v Ananya Iyer>But ask why does my deploy hang after the health check, and you got nothing,

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.300
<v Ananya Iyer>because the runbook says readiness probe timeout.

7
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.540
<v Ananya Iyer>Semantic search was the mirror image. It understood the question,

8
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.120
<v Ananya Iyer>but it would rank a general page about probes above the one runbook that mentioned E4031.

9
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.400
<v Ananya Iyer>So we stopped choosing. We run both queries in Elasticsearch:

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.140
<v Ananya Iyer>BM25 for the words, and a k-nearest-neighbors query over embeddings for the meaning,

11
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.080
<v Ananya Iyer>with the same filters on both.

12
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.920
<v Ananya Iyer>Then we fuse the two ranked lists with reciprocal rank fusion.

13
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:52.040
<v Ananya Iyer>Each document scores one over sixty plus its rank in each list, and the sums decide the order.

14
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.100
<v Ananya Iyer>No tuning, no learned weights.

15
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.440
<v Ananya Iyer>On our forty golden queries, the right page landed in the top five

16
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:02.960
<v Ananya Iyer>sixty-one percent of the time with keywords alone, and eighty-four percent with the hybrid.

17
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.600
<v Ananya Iyer>The cost is two queries instead of one, and that was worth it.
